 "director": {
  "mode": "hand",
  "notes": "Musa is a labelled light drop; the people faceless; the army fades under the closing sea (no drowning bodies). The slaughter of sons (49) is never shown. The calf (51) is never drawn. Glosses avoid Al-Muyassar's first-person paraphrases. STAGING v4: 49 stays ambient (the slaughter of sons is never shown); the chains now end before «ربكم». 50: the sea parts, the Children of Israel cross; Pharaoh (labelled) and his soldiers enter the paths after them (Muyassar: فلما دخل فرعون وجنوده طرقكم) and leave the stage before the water covers the place on «وأغرقنا»; the Children of Israel walk to the mouth of the dry path and fade into it (on «البحر») before the army appears; the soldiers walk into the path and fade there with Pharaoh, so nobody is under the water. Musa is not drawn here: neither 2:50 nor its two tafsirs name him (the earlier version had him). 51-52: Musa (blue drop) leaves for the appointment of forty nights, the people turn away on «اتخذتم» (the calf is never drawn), Musa returns before the pardon (Muyassar: بعد عودة موسى) and the people bow on «عفونا»."
 },
